{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945328-rolling-to-remain-active","id":945328,"title":"Rolling to remain active","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-07T00:02:40-07:00","id":945328,"title":"Rolling to remain active","content":"Hi, I hope you're having a good day everyone.<br /> I was wondering. If you like inflicted say 11 aggravated damage to a wolf and he got like 2 successes on soaking roll. say 6 agg killed him, he can just ignore the 3 aggravated damage left and still roll rage to remain active or he must roll, get at least 4 successes to heal those 3 health levels + 1 to remain active? I'm kinda confused about it and I'm not an expert in WTA.<br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:19:55-07:00","id":945335,"title":"","content":"He's dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T03:47:11-07:00","id":945391,"title":"","content":"It depends a bit on edition, since the phrasing varies a bit between them.<br /> <br /> The most technical reading would suggest that you only ever need one success to survive, because the system doesn't continue to track damage after the &quot;dead&quot; level. You don't keep recording damage after Incapacitated + 1, so 1 success if you're &quot;dead&quot; moves you to Incapacitated, or 2 successes when dead/1 success while Incapacitated moves you to Crippled and combat capable again.<br /> <br /> Forcing people to track makes more sense when massive damage is involved though. The idea that a werewolf can survive 10 Agg with one success is one thing, but 100 Agg would mean something magnitudes more potent (though would seem to be in the, &quot;why are we even rolling?&quot; point). <br /> <br /> Realistically speaking though, it doesn't really change much. Snapping back up to Crippled doesn't really bode well for surviving the fight since 1 more Agg and you're dead for good. In all my WtA games, Remaining Active has been at least as likely to result in a &quot;going out with a blaze of glory&quot; attack before dying for good, than the odds for actually using it to survive a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T08:07:12-07:00","id":945463,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what Heavy Arms said. The wording can be a bit unclear, though I personally generally track below Dead and would have the player have to get 4 successes.<br /> Werewolves are incredibly resilient to begin with and don't necessarily need the additional benefit of coming back from an overwhelming hit like that.<br /> <br /> Mind you, this isn't necessary and if you want the player to just roll at least 1 success, and tick up from there, that would be a fine interpretation of the rules imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T20:35:52-07:00","id":945889,"title":"","content":"The six levels of aggravated damage will drop the player to the incapacitated. One success is required in the remaining active roll for him to spring back into an outrageous berserk frenzy. However, this last-ditch survival effort has its price. Like all Rage rolls, the character is still subject to frenzy. The wound will also remain on the Garou\u2019s body as an appropriate Battle Scar (unless a gift such as Mother's Touch was used onto the said wolf quite recently, it will heal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T01:39:48-07:00","id":946016,"title":"","content":"I usually ignore all damage that is beyond the usual health levels, when a werecreature is injured. If the creature is rolling to remain active then the first success removes 'Incapacitated'.<br /> <br /> If damage didn't come from a mechanical source but a story element, I choose to net let the player role. Meaning, there are some situations beyond rolling dice. If the garou is hit by a high velocity train, or a massive explosion, or decapitated than the werebeast is dead. But beyond that, damage stops at Incapacitated and I as ST determine what happens. To kill a werebeast I usually require another character to use an additional action to set a death blow to an incapacitated being (although usually no roll is required for brawl or melee).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:55:35-07:00","id":946481,"title":"","content":"When i have ran, i always track damage below, so when they roll, they must 'rage heal' as many as they are below incap +1..<br /> Of the St's i have played under, 3 were also like that, 5 were not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:03:09-07:00","id":948491,"title":"","content":"Ok uh, to strike a wolf's neck/head either in his crinos - hispo, how many successes needed for that and can he roll rage to remain active with a supercharge regeneration and grow a new head? xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:32:27-07:00","id":948511,"title":"","content":"The combat system is more abstract than that and there isn't really a rule for aiming at the neck. At least I could not find one browsing through W20.<br /> In general I'd say decapitation would not allow a remain active roll, but I would not allow something like that to happen in combat.<br /> If, outside of combat, a character manages to get his head in a guillotine, though luck.<br /> <br /> In almost all cases, remaining active via rage is okay in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T06:36:15-07:00","id":948564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945328-rolling-to-remain-active?p=948491#post948491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok uh, to strike a wolf's neck/head either in his crinos - hispo, how many successes needed for that and can he roll rage to remain active with a supercharge regeneration and grow a new head? xD</div> </div> </div> </div>In a game I was in something like this happened. Effectively the roll to remain active healed the would behind the blade, leaving a battlescar across the Garou's neck.<br /> The description worked cinematically. Admittedly I can see it not working in all games.<br /> I agree though that something like a guillotine would just leave you dead since you can't heal through a metal sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T22:21:02-07:00","id":949125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945328-rolling-to-remain-active?p=948491#post948491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok uh, to strike a wolf's neck/head either in his crinos - hispo, how many successes needed for that and can he roll rage to remain active with a supercharge regeneration and grow a new head? xD</div> </div> </div> </div>You can ask your storyteller, there are many creative ways they could come up with in order to overcome such an issue and come to a more &quot;realistic&quot; touch when interpreting that. I agree with heinrich I definitely wouldn't allow such a thing in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","user":"Darko","date":". 08-12-2016, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T22:41:27-07:00","id":949135,"title":"","content":"I've seen some 'head/neck' shots, but all were at least at +3 to the base diff, and needed 3+ successes AFTER dodging/parrying..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}